---
title: Cinnamon Apple Cake
description: A cream cheese cake full of chopped apples, with a cinnamon sugar crust.
tags: [cake, baking]
course: dessert
servings: 6-8
time: 2h45m
---

Preheat the oven to 350°F (175°C).

Combine the @all-purpose flour{180%g}(1 1/2 cups), @baking powder{1 1/2%tsp}, and @salt{1/2%tsp}.

Beat the @sugar{297%g}(1 1/2 cups), @butter{112%g}(1/2 cup, softened, or margarine or a combo), @vanilla extract{1%tsp}, and @cream cheese{6%oz}(170 g, block-style, softened, about 3/4 cup) at medium speed of a #mixer{} until well blended (about ~beat{4%minutes}).

Add the @eggs{2}(large), one at a time, beating well after each addition.

Add the flour mixture to the creamed mixture, beating at low speed until blended.

Combine the @&sugar{50%g} and @ground cinnamon{2%tsp}.

Combine 2 tbsp of the cinnamon mixture and the @apples{340%g}(about 3 cups, chopped, peeled) in a #bowl{}, and stir the apple mixture into the batter.

Pour the batter into an 8-inch #springform pan{} that has been greased and floured. Sprinkle the batter with the remaining cinnamon mixture.

> You can also make this cake in a 9-inch square cake pan or a 9-inch springform pan; just reduce the cooking time by 5 minutes.

Bake at 350°F (175°C) for ~bake{75%minutes} or until the cake pulls away from the sides of the pan. Cool the cake completely on a #wire rack{}, and cut with a #serrated knife{}.
